---
title: One pass of SizingLoopL2, in call order
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant L as SizingLoopL2
    participant G as geom
    participant T as tail
    participant P as prop
    participant C as con
    participant A as aero
    participant M as miss
    participant W as wts

    Note over L: state going in: W0, T_SL, WS, TW

    L->>G: S_ref = W0 / WS
    Note right of G: every Dependent geometry property<br/>recomputes on the next read:<br/>span, chords, exposed areas, S_wet

    L->>T: size()
    T->>G: read S_ref, b_wing, cbar_wing, L_fus
    T-->>L: S_ht, S_vt
    L->>G: write S_ht, S_vt

    L->>P: T_SL = T_SL
    Note right of P: this reaches geom too:<br/>nacelle diameter is Dependent on T_SL

    L->>C: optimal_point_continuous([WS, TW])
    C->>A: drag_polar(state)
    A->>G: read S_ref, S_wet, AR, sweeps
    A-->>C: CD0, K1, K2
    C->>P: get_thrust_lapse(state)
    P-->>C: alpha
    C-->>L: WS, TW
    Note over L: T_SL_new = TW * W0

    L->>M: total_fuel(W0)
    M->>A: drag_polar per segment
    M->>G: get_S_ref()
    M->>P: TSFC, thrust
    M-->>L: W_fuel, breakdown

    L->>W: get_OEW(W0)
    W->>G: read exposed areas, S_ht, S_vt
    W->>P: read T_SL for the engine weight
    W-->>L: W_OEW

    Note over L: W0_new = W_payload / (1 - W_OEW/W0 - W_fuel/W0)
    Note over L: under-relax BOTH states, then go again
